@startuml
title squatm3gator System Architecture
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 200

actor "Web User" as User

node "Client Browser" as Browser {
  component "Web UI\n(index.html)" as WebUI
  component "WebSocket Client" as WSClient
}

node "API Server Process" as APIServer {
  component "HTTP API\n- GET /\n- GET /homoglyphs/complete?domain=...\n- Error handling (400/404/500)\n- Session validation" as HTTPAPI
  component "WebSocket Gateway\n(Socket.IO/WebSocket)" as WSGateway
  component "Option Builder\n- Parse attack codes: Hf, Hc, -add, F, R\n- Flags: godaddy, output\n- Build CLI opts (e.g., -Hf, --add, --output=json)" as OptionBuilder
  component "Session Manager\n- Create session on GET /\n- Session ID == Job ID" as SessionMgr
  component "Background Consumer Thread\n- Started by API process" as Consumer
}

component "Redis Job Channel" <<queue>> as RedisJobs
component "Redis Report Channel" <<queue>> as RedisReports

node "Worker Execution" as Worker {
  component "Worker Adapter\n- Receive jobs\n- Invoke engine\n- Stream progress/results" as WorkerAdapter
  component "Subprocess: squatm3 CLI\n(domain-generation engine)" as Squatm3
}

cloud "GoDaddy APIs" as GoDaddy {
  component "Availability Endpoints" as GoDaddyEP
}

component "Configuration\n- Redis URI\n- GoDaddy key/secret/base URL/endpoints" as Config

User --> WebUI : Use main page
Browser --> HTTPAPI : HTTP GET /\n(create session)
HTTPAPI --> SessionMgr : Create/validate session
HTTPAPI --> WebUI : Render index.html
Browser --> HTTPAPI : GET homoglyphs (complete)\nwith domain and options
HTTPAPI --> OptionBuilder : Build attack/options
HTTPAPI --> RedisJobs : Publish job\n(Job ID = Session ID)
WSClient <--> WSGateway : WebSocket channel\n(session-bound updates)

Consumer ..> RedisJobs : Subscribe/listen for jobs
Consumer --> WorkerAdapter : Dispatch job for execution
WorkerAdapter --> Squatm3 : Run with options
WorkerAdapter --> RedisReports : Publish report messages

WSGateway ..> RedisReports : Subscribe to reports
WSGateway --> WSClient : Emit only messages\nmatching session key

WorkerAdapter --> GoDaddyEP : Optional availability queries\nAuthorization: sso-key key:secret

APIServer --> Config : Read runtime config
WorkerAdapter --> Config : Read GoDaddy endpoints
HTTPAPI --> Config : Read Redis URI and options

note right of RedisReports
Report format:
WORKER_ID#JOB_UUID#{MESSAGE/RESULT}
Only messages where JOB_UUID == Session ID
end note

note bottom of OptionBuilder
Option rules:
- Supported codes: Hf, Hc, -add, F, R
- Prefix values with '-' (Hf -> -Hf)
- For '-add' emit '--add'
- If godaddy==1 add GoDaddy option
- If output==1 add --output=json
end note

note bottom of Consumer
Constraint C-003:
Background consumer is started by API process
and listens on Redis job channel
end note

note bottom of HTTPAPI
FR-007/FR-008:
Return plain-text messages for 400/404/500
and parsing failures
end note
@enduml
